---
import Legal from '../../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { me } from '../../../data.js';

const title = 'GrammarLens support';
const description = 'How to get help with GrammarLens, report a bug, or ask a question.';
const updated = '16 October 2026';
---

<Legal title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>Support</strong>
      GrammarLens for iOS<br />
      Last updated: {updated}
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h1 class="display">Support</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Write to <a href={`mailto:${me.email}`}>{me.email}</a>. Include your device model and iOS version — it
        usually saves a round trip. Expect a reply within five business days.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>Common questions</strong>
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <h2 class="h3">How do I cancel my subscription?</h2>
      <p>
        In iOS Settings, tap your name, then Subscriptions, then GrammarLens, then
        Cancel Subscription. Cancelling in the app is not possible — Apple handles all
        subscriptions. Deleting the app does not cancel it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3">I subscribed but the app says I am not Premium.</h2>
      <p>
        On Home, tap Premium next to Topic practice, then tap Restore Purchases at the
        bottom of that screen. If that does not work, make sure you are signed in to the
        same Apple ID you subscribed with, then write to us.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3">Was I charged after the free trial?</h2>
      <p>
        The trial converts to a paid subscription unless you cancel at least 24 hours
        before it ends. Refunds are handled by Apple: <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">report a problem</a> at Apple's site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3">The app says I have reached my daily limit.</h2>
      <p>
        Each installation can generate a limited number of exercises per day, which is
        what keeps the service running. The limit resets at midnight UTC.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3">I think the app marked my correct answer as wrong.</h2>
      <p>
        It happens — feedback is AI-generated and is not always right. Send us the
        sentence and what you typed and we will look at it; that is how the scoring gets
        better.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3">Does GrammarLens work offline?</h2>
      <p>
        No. Exercises are generated on demand, so an internet connection is required.
        Your past sessions and progress are stored on your device and are readable
        offline.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3">How do I delete my data?</h2>
      <p>
        Delete the app. That removes everything stored on your phone: your name, your
        avatar and your practice history. There is no account to close. The anonymous
        usage data the app sends, including the learning goal you picked, is never
        linked to your name, so we have no way to find or delete one person's records;
        Google's Firebase removes it under its own retention settings. Our server's
        daily counters delete themselves within 48 hours and its logs within about
        three days. Details are in the <a href="/products/grammarlens/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3">What is free and what needs Premium?</h2>
      <p>
        The app shows the full comparison on its Premium screen, and it always reflects
        what exists today — nothing is listed that is not built.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <aside class="note">
      <strong>Privacy and terms</strong>
    </aside>
    <div class="body">
      <p>
        <a href="/products/grammarlens/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp;
        <a href="/products/grammarlens/terms/">Terms of Service</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp;
        <a href="/products/grammarlens/support/">Support</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Legal>
